the syntax even looks ok :)
its definately much further along feature-wise than pgsql
yes
the pgsql model is sucky
and its very limited
8.2 will be better
ah .. last time i checked there was nothing decidedly on the horizon yet
its kind of unfortunate that this open source db list hasnt really taken off
i was hoping that it could lead to some standardization efforts for non ANSI SQL features
for all open source databases
but the camps are too entrenched
anyways .. the pocket reference i mentioned showed that if you delete all the rows an index matches, the read time remains almost unchanged
which is unsuprising giving how things are implemented
did you know that maxdb requires no maintaince at all? .. in a way you could say its just less &quot;optimized&quot; ..
they do all balancing, deleting etc immediatly
so they get constant speed
which they claim is a big plus for 24/7 shops
hm, for good and bad...
they also do not havy mvcc IIRC
i have faint recollections that they are working on that though
