ah ok
international characters have a tendency to break their output
(its also entered as plain text when you edit your profile)
but yes, its a good point.
I'll put it on the to-do list
I think the only key question remaining is do you want to conflate your physical and SL identities
pseudonyms
conflicts are only likely to arise when you markup your virtual identity with physical properties
e.g. bday
ah
which I didn't really realize until seeing your actual example
(this has been a good exercise)
bday = date account was created, known colloquially as &quot;rezday&quot;
^in this case
indeed. consider that people don't list their AIM or other online accounts as having a &quot;bday&quot; of the date the account was created
my understanding of bday is that it is meant to represent the physical birth date of the entity represented by the vCard/hCard
in practice, Second Life users tend to celebrate their rezday as they would their birthday
there are other analogies for this too - such as the &quot;member since 1998&quot; printing on credit cards
the date of when that specific facet/identity was created
rather than the entity that the facet/identity is a part of
I think they can be considered different concepts
hEvent then ?
