CONVERSATION:
b8810fee2f4a71f849f3f7409546d1d9: yeah, that should probably be changed to point to html4/
hmm... is this valid? &lt;figure&gt;&lt;legend&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: should be, since emptiness is valid prose
cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: however, RELAX NG is unable to make this invalid: &lt;figure&gt;foo&lt;legend&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;bar&lt;/figure&gt;
cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: I'm working on fixing that in Java
ok, so you're aware of v.nu not agreeing with the spec wrt figure... :)
it seems to do the right thing when you put elements in there, but not text or nothing
cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: I wasn't aware that there was a problem with nothingness
Error: Required children missing from element figure.
cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: I had accidentally made it require one prose element instead of prose content
i was about to send an email about empty &lt;tbody&gt;, but it turns out that i had already complained about that twice
heh
cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: fix for nothingness deployed. thanks
whoa. I was wrong about the expressiveness of RELAX NG in this case, apparently
which is nice
notes that &lt;map&gt; now also has a friendlier content model
cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: I implemented that one correctly, didn't I?
yes, afaict
ok
it was a note to self... :) i think i have sent email about that too, before
previously this was not allowed: &lt;map&gt;&lt;area ...&gt;&lt;/map&gt;
I'm positively puzzled and surprised to learn that RELAX NG can deal with &lt;figure&gt;a&lt;legend/&gt;b&lt;/figure&gt;
