But not Firefox 3.5.
Nor Opera
Might be some kind of WebKit bug
If it breaks the site for all Safari users, that means we can't switch the doctype right now.
I'm trying to make a minimal test case.
There's approximately zero benefit in changing the doctype, so it doesn't seem worth hurting users
though I suppose it's nice to make browsers do Standards instead of Almost Standards
Well, the idea is to actually deploy valid HTML 5, which means switching the doctype.
My understanding is that the point of the HTML 5 doctype is to make sure that old content will work.
I think the point is to make old content work the same as if it used an old Standards mode doctype (e.g. XHTML Strict), and also to be as short as possible
Aha.
